    "html": "<p><strong>Dr Ramesh Aravind is an Indian actor, film director, television host, author and motivational speaker.</strong> Since his debut in 1986 he has acted in more than 140 films in Kannada, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi, directed eight feature films, and hosted five seasons of the Kannada talk show <em>Weekend With Ramesh</em> on Zee Kannada.</p>\n<h2>Five careers in one</h2>\n<p>Few people in Indian entertainment work across as many fields as Dr Ramesh Aravind. Each of his roles reaches a different audience:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Role</th>\n<th>What he is known for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Actor</td>\n<td>140+ films since 1986, mostly in Kannada cinema, including <em>America America</em>, <em>Amrutha Varshini</em>, <em>O Mallige</em> and <em>Hoomale</em></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Director</td>\n<td>Eight feature films, from <em>Rama Shama Bhama</em> (2005) to <em>100</em> (2021)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Television host</td>\n<td>Five seasons of <em>Weekend With Ramesh</em> on Zee Kannada; Season 3 of <em>Kannadada Kotyadhipati</em></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Author</td>\n<td><em>Preetiyinda Ramesh</em>, <em>Art of Success</em>, <em>It&#39;s No Fun Without U</em> and the Tamil edition <em>Anbudan Ramesh</em></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Speaker</td>\n<td>Talks in English, Kannada and Tamil for companies, colleges and conferences</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>He is also a screenwriter and a television producer, with serials such as <em>Sundari</em> on Udaya TV and <em>Neenadena</em> and <em>Aase</em> on Star Suvarna.</p>\n<h2>The actor</h2>\n<p>Ramesh Aravind made his debut in the Kannada film <em>Sundara Swapnagalu</em> in 1986. He went on to work in Tamil from 1987 and Telugu from 1988, and became one of the best-known leading men of 1990s Kannada cinema. His performances in <em>America America</em>, <em>Amrutha Varshini</em> and <em>Hoomale</em> won him the Karnataka State Film Award for Best Actor and two Filmfare Awards South for Best Actor – Kannada.</p>\n<p>His later work includes <em>Pushpaka Vimana</em> (2017), the detective films <em>Shivaji Surathkal</em> (2020) and <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em> (2023), and <em>Bhairadevi</em> (2024).</p>\n<h2>The director</h2>\n<p>He moved behind the camera with <em>Rama Shama Bhama</em> (2005), which won him the Udaya Film Award for Best Debut Director. He has since directed films including <em>Accident</em> (2008), the Tamil film <em>Uttama Villain</em> (2015) starring Kamal Haasan, <em>Sundaranga Jaana</em> (2016) and the thriller <em>100</em> (2021).</p>\n<h2>The host, author and speaker</h2>\n<p>For many viewers in Karnataka, he is first and foremost the host of <em>Weekend With Ramesh</em>, a celebrity talk show that revisits the life journeys of achievers from cinema, sport, business and public life. He has also hosted <em>Kannadada Kotyadhipati</em> and was a judge on <em>Mahanati</em> (2024).</p>\n<p>His books carry the same spirit. <em>Preetiyinda Ramesh</em>, his best-known Kannada book, went through five editions in five months. As a motivational speaker he talks about personal growth, leadership, success and overcoming failure, in English, Kannada and Tamil.</p>\n<h2>Why he is called &quot;Dr&quot;</h2>\n<p>In 2022, Rani Channamma University in Belagavi awarded Ramesh Aravind an honorary doctorate for his contribution to cinema. Since then he has been known as Dr Ramesh Aravind.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Where is Ramesh Aravind from?</h3>\n<p>He was born on 10 September 1964 in Kumbakonam, Tamil Nadu, and lives and works in Bengaluru, Karnataka.</p>\n<h3>How many films has Ramesh Aravind acted in?</h3>\n<p>More than 140 films in Kannada, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi since 1986.</p>\n<h3>What TV show is Ramesh Aravind best known for?</h3>\n<p><em>Weekend With Ramesh</em>, the Kannada celebrity talk show he hosted for five seasons on Zee Kannada.</p>\n<h2>Related pages</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/ramesh-aravind-biography\">Biography of Dr Ramesh Aravind</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/movies\">Movies and filmography</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/television-shows\">TV shows</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/contact\">Contact and bookings</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.ramesharavind.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.ramesharavind.com</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0712076/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0712076/</a></li>\n</ul>\n"
