    "html": "<p><strong>Ramesh Aravind has acted in more than 140 films in Kannada, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi since 1986, and has directed eight.</strong> This guide groups his best-known films by period and role, from his debut in <em>Sundara Swapnagalu</em> to recent work such as <em>100</em> (2021), <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em> (2023) and <em>Bhairadevi</em> (2024).</p>\n<h2>How to read his filmography</h2>\n<p>With more than 140 films, it helps to think of his career in phases:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1986–1993:</strong> debuts in Kannada, Tamil and Telugu</li>\n<li><strong>1994–2004:</strong> leading man in Kannada and Tamil cinema, and his biggest award-winning roles</li>\n<li><strong>2005–2016:</strong> director as well as actor</li>\n<li><strong>2017 onwards:</strong> thrillers, character roles and recent directing work</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The tables below list selected films. For the complete list, see the <a href=\"/movies\">movies page</a>.</p>\n<h2>Early films and debuts (1986–1995)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Film</th>\n<th>Year</th>\n<th>Language</th>\n<th>Role</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><em>Sundara Swapnagalu</em></td>\n<td>1986</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor (debut)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Rudraveena</em></td>\n<td>1988</td>\n<td>Telugu</td>\n<td>Actor (Telugu debut)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Duet</em></td>\n<td>1994</td>\n<td>Tamil</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Sathi Leelavathi</em></td>\n<td>1995</td>\n<td>Tamil</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>His Tamil debut, <em>Manathil Uruthi Vendum</em>, came in 1987.</p>\n<h2>Award-winning Kannada years (1997–2004)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Film</th>\n<th>Year</th>\n<th>Language</th>\n<th>Role</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><em>America America</em></td>\n<td>1997</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Amrutha Varshini</em></td>\n<td>1997</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>O Mallige</em></td>\n<td>1997</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Nammoora Mandara Hoove</em></td>\n<td>1997</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Hoomale</em></td>\n<td>1998</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor, writer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Bhoomi Thayiya Chochhala Maga</em></td>\n<td>1998</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Kotigalu Saar Kotigalu</em></td>\n<td>2001</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Panchatanthiram</em></td>\n<td>2002</td>\n<td>Tamil</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Apthamitra</em></td>\n<td>2004</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n<td>Actor</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>This period brought him the Karnataka State Film Award for Best Actor (<em>America America</em>), the Filmfare Award South for Best Actor – Kannada for <em>Amrutha Varshini</em> and <em>Hoomale</em>, and the Udaya Film Award for Best Actor for <em>O Mallige</em>.</p>\n<h2>Films he directed</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Film</th>\n<th>Year</th>\n<th>Language</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><em>Rama Shama Bhama</em></td>\n<td>2005</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Sathyavan Savithri</em></td>\n<td>2007</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Accident</em></td>\n<td>2008</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Venkata in Sankata</em></td>\n<td>2009</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Nammanna Don</em></td>\n<td>2012</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Uttama Villain</em></td>\n<td>2015</td>\n<td>Tamil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Sundaranga Jaana</em></td>\n<td>2016</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>100</em></td>\n<td>2021</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>He also acted in several of these, including <em>Rama Shama Bhama</em>, <em>Accident</em> and <em>100</em>. <em>Rama Shama Bhama</em> won him the Udaya Film Award for Best Debut Director.</p>\n<h2>Recent films as an actor</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Film</th>\n<th>Year</th>\n<th>Director</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><em>Pushpaka Vimana</em></td>\n<td>2017</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Shivaji Surathkal</em></td>\n<td>2020</td>\n<td>Akash Srivatsa</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em></td>\n<td>2023</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Bhairadevi</em></td>\n<td>2024</td>\n<td>Shreeji</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>His role as the detective in <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em> won him the Chandanavana Film Critics Academy Award for Best Actor in 2024.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How many movies has Ramesh Aravind done?</h3>\n<p>More than 140 films as an actor since 1986, and eight as a director.</p>\n<h3>Which languages has Ramesh Aravind acted in?</h3>\n<p>Kannada, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi, with most of his work in Kannada cinema.</p>\n<h3>What are Ramesh Aravind&#39;s recent films?</h3>\n<p>Recent films include <em>100</em> (2021), which he directed, <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em> (2023) and <em>Bhairadevi</em> (2024).</p>\n<h2>Related pages</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/movies\">Full movies list</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/director-portfolio\">Films as director</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/awards\">Awards and honours</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.ramesharavind.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.ramesharavind.com</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0712076/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0712076/</a></li>\n</ul>\n"
