    "html": "<p><strong>The Kannada film 100 (2021) was written and directed by Ramesh Aravind, who also plays the lead role.</strong> It is a tense cat-and-mouse thriller between a determined police officer and a dangerous cyberstalker, co-starring Shamna Kasim and Rachita Ram. It is the most recent of the eight films he has directed.</p>\n<h2>The story</h2>\n<p><em>100</em> is built around a threat that almost every family now understands: harassment that arrives through a phone or a screen. A police officer finds himself in a battle of wits with a cyberstalker, and the film follows the chase as it becomes increasingly personal and urgent.</p>\n<p>Its subject keeps the thriller grounded. The danger in <em>100</em> is not a distant crime; it is the kind of digital intrusion that viewers recognise from news stories and their own lives.</p>\n<h2>Credits</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Credit</th>\n<th>Name</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Director</td>\n<td>Ramesh Aravind</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Writer</td>\n<td>Ramesh Aravind</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stars</td>\n<td>Ramesh Aravind, Shamna Kasim, Rachita Ram</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Language</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Year</td>\n<td>2021</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>On <em>100</em>, Ramesh Aravind was writer, director and lead actor, holding the story together from the script stage to the final performance.</p>\n<h2>A change of genre</h2>\n<p>Ramesh Aravind&#39;s films as a director cover a wide range. His debut, <em>Rama Shama Bhama</em> (2005), was a comedy of complications. <em>Accident</em> (2008) was a drama about a man questioning the circumstances of his activist wife&#39;s death. <em>Uttama Villain</em> (2015) was a Tamil film about legacy and art.</p>\n<p><em>100</em> takes him into the contemporary thriller: faster, darker and built on suspense. It also fits a wider shift in his recent acting work towards investigative roles, including the detective Shivaji Surathkal in <em>Shivaji Surathkal</em> (2020) and <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em> (2023), directed by Akash Srivatsa.</p>\n<h2>Where 100 sits in his directing career</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Film</th>\n<th>Year</th>\n<th>Language</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Rama Shama Bhama</td>\n<td>2005</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sathyavan Savithri</td>\n<td>2007</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Accident</td>\n<td>2008</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Venkata in Sankata</td>\n<td>2009</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nammanna Don</td>\n<td>2012</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uttama Villain</td>\n<td>2015</td>\n<td>Tamil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sundaranga Jaana</td>\n<td>2016</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>100</strong></td>\n<td><strong>2021</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Kannada</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>A note on the release year</h2>\n<p><em>100</em> was released in <strong>2021</strong>. Some older listings online give a different year; 2021 is the correct release year.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Who directed the Kannada film 100?</h3>\n<p>Ramesh Aravind wrote and directed <em>100</em> (2021), and he also plays the lead role.</p>\n<h3>Who acted in the film 100?</h3>\n<p>The film stars Ramesh Aravind, Shamna Kasim and Rachita Ram.</p>\n<h3>What is the film 100 about?</h3>\n<p>It is a thriller about a police officer locked in a cat-and-mouse battle with a dangerous cyberstalker.</p>\n<h2>Related pages</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/director-portfolio\">Film director – Dr Ramesh Aravind</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/movies\">Movies &amp; filmography</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/ramesh-aravind-biography\">Biography</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wikipedia – Ramesh Aravind</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.ramesharavind.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Official website – www.ramesharavind.com</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0712076/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">IMDb – Ramesh Aravind</a></li>\n</ul>\n"
