    "slug": "ramesh-aravind-awards-and-honours",
    "title": "Ramesh Aravind Awards and Honours: The Complete List",
    "description": "Every major award won by Dr Ramesh Aravind: Karnataka State Film Award, two Filmfare Awards South, Udaya awards and his 2022 honorary doctorate.",
    "question": "What awards has Ramesh Aravind won?",
    "keywords": [
      "Ramesh Aravind awards",
      "Ramesh Aravind Filmfare",
      "Ramesh Aravind Karnataka State Film Award",
      "Ramesh Aravind honours",
      "Udaya Film Awards Ramesh Aravind",
      "Ramesh Aravind best actor"
    ],
    "html": "<p><strong>Dr Ramesh Aravind has won the Karnataka State Film Award for Best Actor, two Filmfare Awards South for Best Actor – Kannada, and the Udaya Film Award for Best Debut Director.</strong> He has also received a 2024 critics&#39; award for Best Actor and, in 2022, an honorary doctorate from Rani Channamma University.</p>\n<h2>Awards as an actor</h2>\n<p>Most of his acting awards came in the late 1990s, when a run of family dramas made him one of the most watched leading men in Kannada cinema. The same films won him recognition from several different award bodies, which shows how widely those performances were appreciated.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Year</th>\n<th>Award</th>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Film</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>1996–97</td>\n<td>Karnataka State Film Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor</td>\n<td>America America</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1997</td>\n<td>Filmfare Awards South</td>\n<td>Best Actor – Kannada</td>\n<td>Amrutha Varshini</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1997</td>\n<td>Udaya Film Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor</td>\n<td>O Mallige</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1997</td>\n<td>Screen Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor – Kannada</td>\n<td>America America / Amrutha Varshini</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1998</td>\n<td>Filmfare Awards South</td>\n<td>Best Actor – Kannada</td>\n<td>Hoomale</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1998</td>\n<td>Filmfans Association Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor</td>\n<td>Hoomale</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1999</td>\n<td>Filmfans Association Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor</td>\n<td>Sambhrama</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1999</td>\n<td>Cinema Express Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor</td>\n<td>Chandramukhi Pranasakhi</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2006</td>\n<td>Suvarna Film Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor (comedy role)</td>\n<td>Rama Shama Bhama</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2024</td>\n<td>Chandanavana Film Critics Academy Awards</td>\n<td>Best Actor</td>\n<td>Shivaji Surathkal 2</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Two things stand out in this list. First, he won the Filmfare Award South for Best Actor – Kannada in back-to-back years, for <em>Amrutha Varshini</em> (1997) and <em>Hoomale</em> (1998). Second, his recognition is not limited to one era: the 2024 critics&#39; award for <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em> came more than 25 years after his first Filmfare win.</p>\n<h2>Awards as a director and writer</h2>\n<p>Ramesh Aravind&#39;s work behind the camera has also been recognised.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Udaya Film Awards, Best Debut Director (2006)</strong> for <em>Rama Shama Bhama</em>, the first film he directed.</li>\n<li><strong>Raghavendra Prathishtana Awards, Best Story (2005)</strong> for <em>Amrithadhare</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Udaya award is notable because <em>Rama Shama Bhama</em> also earned him the Suvarna Film Award for Best Actor in a comedy role. In other words, the same film was recognised for both his directing and his acting.</p>\n<h2>Honours beyond film awards</h2>\n<p>Alongside film awards, he has received several honours for his wider contribution to Kannada culture and television.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pride of Zee Kannada (2015)</strong>, at the Zee Kutumba Awards</li>\n<li><strong>Nadaprabhu Kempegowda Award (2018)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Dr. Shivarama Karanth Award</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Honorary doctorate (2022)</strong> from Rani Channamma University, Belagavi, for his contribution to cinema</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The honorary doctorate is the reason he is known today as <em>Dr</em> Ramesh Aravind.</p>\n<h2>How to read this list</h2>\n<p>Award lists on fan sites and social media often differ, and some circulate awards that are hard to verify. This page lists only awards that can be checked against public records, including his Wikipedia entry. If you are writing about Ramesh Aravind for a publication, the official <a href=\"/awards\">awards page</a> on his website is the best single reference.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How many Filmfare Awards has Ramesh Aravind won?</h3>\n<p>He has won two Filmfare Awards South for Best Actor – Kannada: for <em>Amrutha Varshini</em> in 1997 and for <em>Hoomale</em> in 1998.</p>\n<h3>Has Ramesh Aravind won a State Award?</h3>\n<p>Yes. He won the Karnataka State Film Award for Best Actor for <em>America America</em> (1996–97).</p>\n<h3>What is Ramesh Aravind&#39;s most recent award?</h3>\n<p>Among his film awards, the most recent is the Chandanavana Film Critics Academy Award for Best Actor (2024) for <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em>.</p>\n<h2>Related pages</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/awards\">Awards &amp; Honours</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/movies\">Movies &amp; Filmography</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/ramesh-aravind-biography\">Biography</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.ramesharavind.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.ramesharavind.com</a></li>\n</ul>\n"
