    "html": "<p><strong>Dr Ramesh Aravind is an Indian actor, film director, television host, author and motivational speaker with more than 140 films since 1986.</strong> These are short, verified answers to the questions people ask most often about him, with links to the official pages that cover each topic in more detail.</p>\n<h2>About him</h2>\n<h3>1. Who is Dr Ramesh Aravind?</h3>\n<p>Dr Ramesh Aravind is an Indian actor, film director, screenwriter, television host, author and motivational speaker. He has acted in more than 140 films in Kannada, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi and is best known on television as the host of <em>Weekend With Ramesh</em> on Zee Kannada.</p>\n<h3>2. When and where was he born?</h3>\n<p>He was born on 10 September 1964 in Kumbakonam, Tamil Nadu. He lives and works in Bengaluru, Karnataka.</p>\n<h3>3. Why is he called &quot;Dr&quot;?</h3>\n<p>Rani Channamma University in Belagavi awarded him an honorary doctorate in 2022 for his contribution to cinema.</p>\n<h3>4. Which languages has he worked in?</h3>\n<p>He has acted in Kannada, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi films. He speaks at events in English, Kannada and Tamil.</p>\n<h2>Films</h2>\n<h3>5. What was his first film?</h3>\n<p>His first film was the Kannada film <em>Sundara Swapnagalu</em> (1986). His Tamil debut was <em>Manathil Uruthi Vendum</em> (1987) and his Telugu debut was <em>Rudraveena</em> (1988).</p>\n<h3>6. How many films has he acted in?</h3>\n<p>More than 140 films across four languages.</p>\n<h3>7. What are his best-known films?</h3>\n<p>As an actor: <em>America America</em>, <em>Amrutha Varshini</em> (1997), <em>O Mallige</em> (1997), <em>Hoomale</em> (1998), <em>Pushpaka Vimana</em> (2017), <em>Shivaji Surathkal</em> (2020) and <em>Shivaji Surathkal 2</em> (2023). See the <a href=\"/movies\">movies page</a>.</p>\n<h3>8. Which films has he directed?</h3>\n<p>Eight feature films:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Film</th>\n<th>Year</th>\n<th>Language</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Rama Shama Bhama</td>\n<td>2005</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sathyavan Savithri</td>\n<td>2007</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Accident</td>\n<td>2008</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Venkata in Sankata</td>\n<td>2009</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nammanna Don</td>\n<td>2012</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uttama Villain</td>\n<td>2015</td>\n<td>Tamil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sundaranga Jaana</td>\n<td>2016</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>2021</td>\n<td>Kannada</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Television</h2>\n<h3>9. What is <em>Weekend With Ramesh</em>?</h3>\n<p>A Kannada celebrity talk show on Zee Kannada, hosted by Dr Ramesh Aravind for five seasons. Each episode revisits the life journey of an achiever from cinema, sport, business or public life.</p>\n<h3>10. What other TV shows has he been part of?</h3>\n<p>He hosted Season 3 of <em>Kannadada Kotyadhipati</em> (the Kannada version of <em>Who Wants to Be a Millionaire</em>), was a judge on <em>Mahanati</em> (Zee Kannada, 2024), and has hosted <em>Raja Rani</em>, <em>Preetiyinda Ramesh</em> and <em>Parichaya</em>. As a producer, his serials include <em>Sundari</em>, <em>Supernatural Fiction</em>, <em>Neenadena</em> and <em>Aase</em>. See the <a href=\"/television-shows\">TV shows page</a>.</p>\n<h2>Books</h2>\n<h3>11. What books has he written?</h3>\n<p>Four books: <em>Preetiyinda Ramesh</em> and <em>Art of Success</em> (Kannada), <em>It&#39;s No Fun Without U</em> (English), and <em>Anbudan Ramesh</em> (Tamil, 2024). He also wrote and narrated the Kannada audiobook <em>MasadaMaatu with Ramesh</em>.</p>\n<h3>12. What is his most popular book?</h3>\n<p><em>Preetiyinda Ramesh</em>, a Kannada bestseller that went through five editions in five months.</p>\n<h2>Awards</h2>\n<h3>13. What awards has he won?</h3>\n<p>His major awards include the Karnataka State Film Award for Best Actor (<em>America America</em>), two Filmfare Awards South for Best Actor – Kannada (<em>Amrutha Varshini</em>, 1997; <em>Hoomale</em>, 1998), the Udaya Film Award for Best Actor (<em>O Mallige</em>, 1997) and the Udaya Film Award for Best Debut Director (<em>Rama Shama Bhama</em>, 2006). The full list is on the <a href=\"/awards\">awards page</a>.</p>\n<h2>Speaking and contact</h2>\n<h3>14. Is he available for motivational talks?</h3>\n<p>Yes. He speaks at corporate events, colleges, literature festivals and community gatherings on personal growth, leadership, success mindset and storytelling. His team replies about availability.</p>\n<h3>15. How can I contact him?</h3>\n<p>Email his team at <strong><a href=\"mailto:enquiry@ramesharavind.com\">enquiry@ramesharavind.com</a></strong> or use the form on the <a href=\"/contact\">contact page</a>. His official social accounts are Instagram @ramesh.aravind.official, X @Ramesh_aravind, YouTube (Ramesh Aravind Official) and Facebook (actor.ramesh.aravind).</p>\n<h2>Related pages</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/ramesh-aravind-biography\">Biography</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/movies\">Movies &amp; Filmography</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/awards\">Awards &amp; Honours</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/contact\">Contact &amp; Bookings</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramesh_Aravind</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.ramesharavind.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.ramesharavind.com</a></li>\n</ul>\n"
